onUniformBallotBitCount Reduce of the ballot of %39 != 0   (cost 32.625 -> 6.875)\n      (line 8: b.d[i] = subgroupExclusiveAdd(x > 5u ? 1u : 0u) + subgroupAdd(x & 1u);)\n      %39 is %28 & 1, in [0, 1] by intervals, so its sum over the lanes is the number of those lanes where it is not 0: the set bits of their ballot, which OpGroupNonUniformBallotBitCount Reduce counts\n      holds for any subgroup size and any set of active lanes: both sides count the active lanes only\n  spirv-val accepts the written module\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 2613 bytes, checksum f7d47a93)\n"}
